"30c10c8aa5c5298d0bc3d4ef84bd3644808a6ab9fed7d1330b974bcb97845612","event_uuid":"526be103-a26a-46ff-85fb-990d96b56bcc","position":{"commit_sha":"c3bb5e25e175cb8b4e174cfcfcae198d0ba2af9c","position":"1794475118362567009-526be103-a26a-46ff-85fb-990d96b56bcc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"67f129790deb8a3d78a623d12a73e32e1b0bda9cee16bb7f64e6efb77deaec33","event_uuid":"a22d6a5b-d2ae-455d-9994-e64c3015fd16","position":{"commit_sha":"9bbbb0c667b012e4799cf13654e3bf1ac36f3bf3","position":"1794475119032513039-a22d6a5b-d2ae-455d-9994-e64c3015fd16"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"1c5b8d1f6fb40b8cacc40fc99472b83e1dc6128ba8bfd14fc14ae69558e6288d","event_uuid":"2cac6e16-5c32-4e3a-9fe1-ba27cb6bf50e","position":{"commit_sha":"9976b7951537f79d5b980210a387c4a6cf523b76","position":"1794475154041987115-2cac6e16-5c32-4e3a-9fe1-ba27cb6bf50e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Reproduced through the real close path, 2026-11-11 ~22:05 PST. transition_ticket(graceless-thievish-olm, in_progress -> closed) over production MCP refused: \"completion verification would read tree aed975de61c788b817028dd82051313c71139d3d (HEAD of /var/gerrit/site/mcp-code), which contains none of the commits the close precheck accepted as this ticket's landed work: b603c4544e893321a109ad81356ba92ea7c05968\". b603c4544e8 (Terraform-only) merged about 40 minutes earlier, and main had since advanced to 6dbf05538f7 (seen in the plan-review attestation's verified_at_sha); the workspace stayed at aed975de61c because neither commit restarted the MCP container. A guard caught the mismatch, so nothing was signed against the wrong tree, but every close of non-MCP-path work fails until the next MCP deploy. Fix c76f28984b9 is in make verify now.","timestamp":1794463040657187099},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fix landed, 2026-11-12 00:40 PST: change 3363 merged as 76ab41f2af9 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, 0 unresolved; make verify rc=0: 21,129 + 218 passed). Tests: test_no_op_tick_refreshes_a_workspace_behind_main reproduces the lag with a real remote advanced by a non-MCP commit and asserts the tick fast-forwards the workspace without paging (verified failing with the refresh call removed); test_current_workspace_is_not_refreshed; the freshness probe is parametrized over current, dirty, diverged, unreadable and absent. Deployed: live rebar-mcp-76ab41f2af98-8093, workspace at 76ab41f2af9 with 0 changes, entrypoint has --refresh-code. Pending: AC3, the live observation that a later non-MCP commit reaches the workspace without a container restart. A bounded poll (about 2 h) is watching for one.","timestamp":1794473083953234157},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"AC3 observed live, 2026-11-12 PST (read-only SSM plus the autodeploy journal). Main advanced from 9489d225d09 (the live MCP image) to 0fccb0f20aa \"Move openai trivial slot off gpt-5.4-nano\", which touches only .github/llm-providers/*, docs/ci-provider-matrix.md and tests/unit/test_ci_provider_matrix.py, no MCP image path. At 01:05:55 PST autodeploy logged `mcp code workspace: refreshed rebar-mcp-9489d225d09a-8092 from 9489d225d09a6df732292f35f49c69cc5fc43418 toward 0fccb0f20aab6b86fe212ad0ae4513776881d7c9`. At 01:08 PST the container was still rebar-mcp-9489d225d09a-8092 (no restart), its MCP_CODE_DIR HEAD was 0fccb0f20aa == /var/lib/rebar/deployed-sha == origin/main, and there were no mcp-code-workspace-stuck markers. Before the fix the same situation stranded the workspace (see the graceless-thievish-olm close refusal above).","timestamp":1794474539842593763},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-12 ~01:20 PST: CLOSED (class preexisting, completion signature signed). The close used no `ref=`. Its completion verdict verified against 0fccb0f20aa, a non-MCP commit that was origin/main at the time, with ran_model bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5, through the in-place refreshed workspace of the unrestarted container rebar-mcp-9489d225d09a-8092. Fix: change 3363 (76ab41f2af9).","timestamp":1794475154041987115}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1794446477421621409,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"bb251559-53e8-4402-92ab-bee682b7aaf2","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"6b02-067c-9dbb-47e7"},{"link_uuid":"ca36c1ae-0ca1-4b05-bd21-b753da85dc07","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8806-198c-e2d6-46ce"},{"link_uuid":"ef994c76-f882-4076-9b8d-16f5cd05c28c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"bc39-9098-4aa5-48ef"}],"description":"## Observed\n\n- `transition_ticket(closed)` over MCP pins completion verification to `resolve_ref(\"HEAD\", repo_root)` (`src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:146`). The server's repo root is `REBAR_ROOT=/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code`.\n- That workspace is refreshed (fetch plus fast-forward) only by `infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh` at container start.\n- Autodeploy restarts the MCP container only when `MCP_PATHS` change (`infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:87`; `src/rebar`, the Dockerfile, the entrypoint, the compose file, `uv.lock`, `pyproject.toml`). A commit touching only docs, tests, `infra/terraform` or other paths advances main without refreshing the workspace.\n- Reproduced 2026-11-11 21:50 PST (read-only SSM): main was b603c4544e8, a Terraform-only commit (infra/terraform/monitoring_bedrock_cost.tf); the live container rebar-mcp-aed975de61c7-8093 had MCP_CODE_DIR HEAD aed975de61c, one commit behind. A close over MCP in that window verifies against aed975de61c, and the close precheck cannot see b603c4544e8.\n\n## Approach\n\nRefresh the live workspace in place on the steady-state autodeploy tick, rather than changing which ref the close resolves (local CLI closes must keep verifying the caller's worktree HEAD).\n- `infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh` gains a `--refresh-code` mode that runs the existing `refresh_code` (locked; refuses dirty or diverged trees; recovers an interrupted fast-forward).\n- `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`: on the no-op tick, `mcp_refresh_code_workspace` reads the live backend's workspace HEAD and, when it is not `$TARGET`, runs `docker exec <live> sh /usr/local/bin/mcp-entrypoint.sh --refresh-code` (bounded at 300 s, like the mirror fetch). The freshness probe then checks that the workspace contains `$TARGET` (not merely the image commit), so a refresh that fails pages through the existing deploy_errors alarm.\n- No config key, env var or flag.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] A test reproduces the lag (workspace at an older commit, main advanced with no MCP image change) and shows the no-op tick fast-forwards it to the target without paging; a test shows a current workspace is not touched. Pinned in `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py`.\n- [x] `make verify` passes and the change lands through Gerrit.\n- [x] [non-codebase] After deploy, a non-MCP-path commit on main reaches the live workspace within a few autodeploy ticks without a container restart.\n  provenance: environment=production rebar host i-00880b2c7f13527c5 (MCP container); principal=frontier operator role via SSM; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — read-only SSM read of MCP_CODE_DIR HEAD vs origin/main and the container name before and after a non-MCP commit lands","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","reason":"in-place workspace refresh on the no-op tick"},{"path":"infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh","reason":"--refresh-code mode"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md","reason":"runbook"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py","reason":"reproduce lag, refresh tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["parent","9794-4336-5ed6-4561"],["relates_to","8806-198c-e2d6-46ce"],["relates_to","bc39-9098-4aa5-48ef"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"9794-4336-5ed6-4561","parent_status_uuid":"526be103-a26a-46ff-85fb-990d96b56bcc","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"0bc1-00c3-3c83-4792","ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP close-gate verifies against a code workspace refreshed only at container start, so it lags main between MCP deploys","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["3aff6050-6d75-4884-936f-7d6b4d62625f","f2d0916d-248c-4bd7-8671-5173f55aeb83","527f6eb4-62a5-4d0a-be9d-c1c246aac698","9593e093-0f70-4483-9834-09b5ec39e0a5","6502e861-7c1b-40d8-b996-f3418b2e3bb9","ef994c76-f882-4076-9b8d-16f5cd05c28c","b92693a7-ea0d-481b-a015-8c1ecb563d7f","def0b695-60f7-4f7e-88b2-c21f7b9831d4","5279a5da-eb34-4b5b-965a-0d8ab0c30307","77867dd5-aa38-4742-b908-9ffa4999d17a","526be103-a26a-46ff-85fb-990d96b56bcc","a22d6a5b-d2ae-455d-9994-e64c3015fd16","2cac6e16-5c32-4e3a-9fe1-ba27cb6bf50e"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794475154041987116,"uuid":"5f95e6b6-445d-4d82-918c-b82ed9a60a09"}